    fix(cp): append newline when forwarding CLI input, shell_task.c strips it

    Confirmed via hardware log: after fixing the dev->recv misuse (previous
    commit), the forwarded characters DID reach AP-side NuttX -- visible as an
    'ap0: nxcamera' echo line in the serial log -- but the command never
    executed (no nxcamera> sub-prompt), because nsh's line editor waits for a
    newline before submitting a buffered line for execution.

    Root cause: shell_task.c's rx_ind_process() strips the terminating '\r'/'\n'
    from cmd_line_buf.cmd_buff before calling handle_shell_input() -- it writes
    a '\0' there instead (see that function's CMD_TYPE_TEXT branch for '\n'/
    '\r'). So ap_uart0_rx_forward() was only ever given the bare command text
    with no newline, which nsh receives and echoes but never submits.

    Fix: append a single '\n' after the caller-supplied bytes before sending,
    so the forwarded line reproduces a real Enter keypress on the AP console.

